  "query_preview": "..\nToday: A zonal A zonal flow pattern will be over the region \ntoday. It will bring a gradual increase in the upper level \nmoisture. Precipitable water values will increase from 0.3-0.5 \nof an inch to 0.6-0.0 of an inch. It will be a precursor to the \nincoming weak Atmospheric River event expected on Tuesday. Highs\nfor the day will be slightly 60s to low 70s. Overnight lows \nwill be warmer than previous nights with 40s to low 50s range. \n\nTuesday: A weak atmospheric river will push into the region. \nThe main impact for many will be gusty winds as the rain shadow \neffect will limit precip across the basin. Ensembles are is \ndecent agreement for the period. Precipitable water increases to\n150-200 percent of normal. Rains will be highest along the \nCascade crest with around 0.50 to 1.00 inch of rain, with light\nrain spilling over the crest into the upper reaches of the \nMethow Valley, Lake Chelan, and Lake Wenatchee. Weaker chances \nextend over the higher terrain of Idaho Panhandle. Amounts are \nexpected to have little to no accumulation. The region will be \nsituated just north of the Canadian border. With speeds near 140\nkts, The Cascade ridges has potential of gusts into 40-50 mph \nrange. Winds will reach into the basin during the afternoon with\ngusts into the 20-30 mph range. Highs will be in the 60 to low \n70s. Overnight lows will be a little cooler with a upper 30s to \n40 range.\n\nWednesday through Saturday: High pressure off the southern \nCalifornia coast will nudge a ridge into the Pacific Northwest. \nIt will bring a warm, dry quiet period for the region. Ensembles\ndiffer on the timing of the strongest period of the the ridge. \nHighs will be in the 70s. Lows will be in the upper 30s and \n40s. /JDC",
